<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lifan Yuan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1638–1906</span> · Also known as Court of Colonial Affairs</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lifan Yuan, or Court of Colonial Affairs, was the Qing government office that managed relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongolia">Mongolia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xinjiang">Xinjiang</a> and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inner-asia">Inner Asian</a> dependencies. Founded in 1638 from the Mongol Office of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> state, it supervised the Mongol nobility and banners, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibetan-buddhism">Tibetan Buddhist</a> affairs and early relations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. In 1906 it was reorganised as the Lifan Bu, a ministry.</p></div>
